  "reason": "The records provide scattered, directionally relevant ideas: HEAs need not exhibit sluggish diffusion (R1, R3, R11), surface or interfacial energetics can control behavior (R2), segregation can occur (R16), kinetic constraints can override equilibrium phase preferences (R5), and temperature can alter HEA structures and properties (R12, R14, R20). However, none describes vacuum heating of multicomponent noble-metal HEA nanoparticles, Au/Cu surface segregation driven by surface-energy differences, morphology-enhanced diffusion, or selective melting/evaporation. An expert could infer that heating and surface energetics merit investigation, but proposing the specific nanoparticle experiment and mechanism would require a substantial new idea."
